37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"It... it seems we have some real problems. I found that people are losing nearly an hour every day just copying records that already exist, and misrouted deliveries are happening because of inconsistent addresses. It feels like a lot of wasted effort.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh, that sounds like a nightmare, @Daisuke! But wait until you hear my news. Our in-house developers are totally booked until Q3, and the coordination group is basically a ghost town! It's a total mess.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,It seems we are discovering a symphony of incompetence. My findings show that half of our customer plants have sporadic network coverage and visitor approvals take six weeks. We are essentially planning for a digital utopia that doesn't exist.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial situation is equally precarious. The capital budget is frozen, meaning we cannot afford new infrastructure. Furthermore, per-head licensing costs will escalate as we scale, while only fixed-fee work remains stable.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, everyone found some really scary stuff! I found out that big projects where everyone has to enter data every day just get ignored and dropped. But the small, specific tools for one trade and the tool room walkthroughs are still being used!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with @Kenji. If people are already exhausted from copying records for an hour a day, they won't have the energy for a big, demanding project. We should look for something that removes these daily burdens.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, you're preaching to the choir! My findings show the coordination group is basically running on fumes. If we pick a project that needs a lot of hand-holding, those poor souls are going to snap!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""snap"" is a bit vivid, but accurate. Between the ghost town of a coordination group and the six-week wait for site access, any project requiring heavy external coordination is a fantasy. We need something lean.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree that lean is necessary. However, we must also be cautious about the funding source. Since the capital budget is frozen, any project requiring upfront infrastructure is impossible. We must prioritize recurring software allowances and fixed-fee costs.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that makes sense! But we also have to remember that even if we have the money, if the project is too big and asks everyone to do more work, it'll just be dropped like the others were! We need something small and helpful!","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think @Kenji is right. If we choose something that feels like more work, it will just fail. We need a project that actually gives time back to the people on the floor.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Exactly! If we just add more tasks to a team that's already writing logs by hand because they're understaffed, we're just setting them up for failure. We need a win that doesn't cost us our sanity!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, sanity is a luxury we clearly can't afford. Let's be rational: if we ignore the network gaps and the access delays, we're just choosing which way we'd prefer to fail. We need a project with zero external dependencies.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I concur. A project with zero external dependencies is the only rational path. Furthermore, we must avoid per-head licensing models that will create an unsustainable financial burden during next year's renewal. Fixed-fee solutions are the only safe bet.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, I totally agree! If we pick something that costs more as it grows, we'll just run out of money. Let's find a project that's small, doesn't need a huge team, and actually helps people without adding more work!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hope we can find something that fits all these needs. If we can find a project that fixes the record copying and address errors without needing new hardware or a huge team, it would really help the people who are struggling.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with you, @Daisuke! Let's find a project that's a real gift to the staff, not another chore. If it doesn't need developers or a huge coordination team, it's a winner in my book!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It is charming that you all view this as a search for a ""gift."" Let us be realistic: we are searching for the only option that isn't a suicide mission. If it requires site access or a full developer team, it is dead on arrival.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, your realism is necessary. To summarize, we require a project that avoids the frozen capital budget, bypasses the developer shortage, and utilizes fixed-fee costs to avoid renewal spikes. Only a lean, internally focused tool is viable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm totally on board with that! Let's look for a project that's simple, doesn't need a bunch of people to manage it, and actually sticks around because it's useful. I can't wait to see the candidates!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
