62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think the Supplier Data Hub is the best choice. It directly addresses the address inconsistencies and the time wasted copying records, and it seems like it wouldn't need the network coverage @Shunichi mentioned.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, the Hub sounds useful, but who's going to manage all those shared update procedures? If it's the coordination group, they're already drowning in hand-written logs! I'm leaning toward the Workflow Assistant. It actually saves time!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the Workflow Assistant is a pleasant toy, but let's look at the Field Service App. It specifically mentions synchronization away from the network, which is the only way to survive the dead zones I found.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the Field Service App is a risk. Mobile apps often require significant capital for hardware or per-head licenses that will spike during renewal. The Supplier Data Hub is more stable if it uses fixed-fee work.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, I agree that the Hub sounds stable, but @May is right about the management! My research showed that big projects with shared update procedures usually get dropped. The Training Studio seems way safer because it's a specific tool for a specific need!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I understand @Kenji's point, but the Training Studio doesn't fix the daily struggle of copying records. The Supplier Data Hub would stop the misrouted deliveries and the wasted hours. I think that's more important than the risk of it being dropped.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I love your heart, but we can't ignore the reality! If we pick the Hub and it crashes because nobody has time to update it, we've helped no one. The Workflow Assistant is a dream—it does the boring writing for us!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, a ""dream"" is exactly what we should avoid in a professional setting. The Workflow Assistant is a luxury, not a necessity. The Field Service App is the only one that acknowledges the physical reality of our technicians' environment.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the Field Service App is a liability. It likely requires mobile hardware and per-head licensing, which our frozen capital budget and renewal risks cannot sustain. The Supplier Data Hub is the most rational choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, I see why you like the Hub, but remember that cross-unit standardization efforts usually end up with no owner! The Hub is exactly that kind of project. The Training Studio is a specific tool that actually lasts!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want to pick a ""toy"" or something that doesn't solve the real pain. The people in the depot are losing an hour every day. If we don't fix the data hub, they just keep suffering.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I hear you, but adding a ""Hub"" that needs constant manual updates just adds another chore to their list! The Workflow Assistant actually removes the burden of writing logs and summaries. It's the only one that gives time back!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you are confusing ""giving time back"" with ""automating a meeting."" Let's be honest: the Workflow Assistant is a vanity project. The Field Service App is the only candidate that solves a structural failure. If it's built right, it's a tool, not a chore.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, a tool is only a tool if we can afford to keep it. The Field Service App's dependency on mobile hardware and scaling licenses is a financial impossibility. The Supplier Data Hub is the only logical solution.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, I really want to help @Daisuke's friends in the depot, but the Hub is just too risky! It's a big standardization project, and those always fail. The Training Studio is a specific tool that actually survives!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I can't just ignore the people who are struggling every day. The Supplier Data Hub is the only one that stops the misrouted deliveries and the copying. I'll vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I really want to help too, but we can't ignore the ghost town in coordination! The Workflow Assistant is the only one that actually lightens the load without adding new chores. I vote for the Workflow Assistant!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It is a tragedy that we are choosing between a vanity project and a financial gamble. However, the Field Service App is the only one that respects the actual conditions of the field. I vote for the Field Service App.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The Field Service App is a financial liability, and the Workflow Assistant is a luxury. The Training Studio is too narrow. The Supplier Data Hub is the only rational choice. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I really want to help @Daisuke's friends, but the Hub is just a recipe for failure! It's too big and needs too much coordination. The Training Studio is a specific tool that actually lasts. I vote for the Training Studio!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
